  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find positions of 8s to determine the axis of symmetry\n    eights = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 8]\n    \n    if not eights:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows_8 = [r for r, c in eights]\n    cols_8 = [c for r, c in eights]\n    \n    # Determine the mirror function based on the line of 8s\n    # Check for horizontal line (constant row)\n    if len(set(rows_8)) == 1:\n        axis_row = rows_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (2 * axis_row - r, c)\n    # Check for vertical line (constant col)\n    elif len(set(cols_8)) == 1:\n        axis_col = cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (r, 2 * axis_col - c)\n    # Check for main diagonal (r - c = constant)\n    elif len(set(r - c for r, c in eights)) == 1:\n        k = rows_8[0] - cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (c + k, r - k)\n    # Check for anti-diagonal (r + c = constant)\n    elif len(set(r + c for r, c in eights)) == 1:\n        k = rows_8[0] + cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (k - c, k - r)\n    else:\n        # Fallback: use vertical axis at average column\n        axis_col = round(sum(cols_8) / len(cols_8))\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (r, 2 * axis_col - c)\n    \n    # Create output grid as copy of input\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Fill in missing values based on reflection\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if out[r][c] == 0:\n                mr, mc = mirror(r, c)\n                if 0 <= mr < rows and 0 <= mc < cols:\n                    val = grid[mr][mc]\n                    if val != 0:\n                        out[r][c] = val\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find positions of 8s to determine the axis of symmetry\n    eights = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 8]\n    \n    if not eights:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows_8 = [r for r, c in eights]\n    cols_8 = [c for r, c in eights]\n    \n    # Determine the mirror function based on the line of 8s\n    # Check for horizontal line (constant row)\n    if len(set(rows_8)) == 1:\n        axis_row = rows_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (2 * axis_row - r, c)\n    # Check for vertical line (constant col)\n    elif len(set(cols_8)) == 1:\n        axis_col = cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (r, 2 * axis_col - c)\n    # Check for main diagonal (r - c = constant)\n    elif len(set(r - c for r, c in eights)) == 1:\n        k = rows_8[0] - cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (c + k, r - k)\n    # Check for anti-diagonal (r + c = constant)\n    elif len(set(r + c for r, c in eights)) == 1:\n        k = rows_8[0] + cols_8[0]\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (k - c, k - r)\n    else:\n        # Fallback: use vertical axis at average column\n        axis_col = round(sum(cols_8) / len(cols_8))\n        def mirror(r, c):\n            return (r, 2 * axis_col - c)\n    \n    # Create output grid as copy of input\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Fill in missing values based on reflection\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if out[r][c] == 0:\n                mr, mc = mirror(r, c)\n                if 0 <= mr < rows and 0 <= mc < cols:\n                    val = grid[mr][mc]\n                    if val != 0:\n                        out[r][c] = val\n    return out",
